  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Language updated after Pro-Doc Revision in 2019

1.1: Extent to which federal institutions develop and effectively implement gender sensitive and inclusive policies/regulations ensuring protection and promotion of human rights. Scale: 1: Policies/regulations partially developed.  2: Policies/regulations developed but not implemented. 3: Policies/regulations developed and partially implemented  

1.2: Extent to which technical capacity of federal institutions is enhanced to enable duty-bearers to effectively deliver on their respective mandates, particularly for women and youth empowerment
Scale: (1: Very Basic Capacity 2: Partial Capacity  3: Capacity Largely in Place)

2.1: Existence of strengthened institutions and systems supporting fulfilment of nationally and internationally ratified human rights obligations: a) Rule of law and justice b) human rights   
Scale 1: Policies/regulations partially developed. 2: Policies/regulations developed but not implemented. 3: Policies/regulations developed and partially implemented

2.2: Technical capacity of provincial institutions on human rights and local governance is enhanced 
Scale:1: Very Basic Capacity 2: Partial Capacity  3: Capacity Largely in Place

3.1: Extent to which LGs are capacitated for provision of inclusive (particularly women) service delivery. Scale: 1: Very Partial Capacity 2: Partial capacity  3: Capacity Largely in Place

4.1: Extent to which citizens oversight enables improved sectoral government action 1: Limited Capacity 2: Very Partial Capacity  3: Partial capacity  4. Capacity largely exist</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2012">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Scale 1 (No capacity)
1.2: Scale item 1: Very Basic Capacity
2.1: Scale 1 (No capacity) (Technical support provided to KP Law Dept. workshops &amp; trainings on HR protection mechanisms)
3.1:  Scale 1 (No capacity) (Cells established in KP only but LGs not operationalized)
4.1: Scale 1 (Not at all)</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Scale 3 [Policies/regulations developed and partially implemented Implementation of National Action Plan recommendations initiated; support provided to NHRIs, including NCHR, NCRC, NCSW; technical assistance provided to implement policies targeting vulnerable groups, particularly persons with disabilities]
1.2: Scale 2: [Capacity development of federal government stakeholders to implement a rights-based approach to development].
2.1: Scale 2: [Policies/regulations developed but not implemented (Support provided for implementation of provincial Social Welfare Department, Local Government and HR policies/plans].
2.2: Scale 2: [Provincial HRIMS stakeholders provided capacity development support; Social inclusion and social protection measures (helplines, shelter homes, referral mechanisms continued in all four provinces; institutionalization of protection measures in partnership with Women Development and Social Welfare Departments].
3.1:Scale 2: [Implementation of short-term recommendations of the socio-economic assessment and COVID-19 task-force recommendations; programme on gender-justice and inclusion of persons with disabilities, and transgenders implemented; community stabilization programme implemented in Balochistan and discussions with government stakeholders on institutional of the model at the local level finalized].
4.1: Scale 2: [Integration Support Groups (ISGs) assisting Social Welfare and Women Development Department in Quetta partially improved engagement between CSOs and government for improved access to services of the most vulnerable and at-risk populations (particularly women, transgenders and youth].</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Scale 3 [Policies/regulations developed and partially implemented implementation of National Action Plan recommendations initiated - federal level steering committee established; trainings on HRDD with Japanese companies initiated; technical and capacity development support provided to NHRIs; detailed study on addressing stigma and discrimination against women with disabilities completed].
1.2: Scale 2: [Capacity development of federal government stakeholders to implement a rights-based approach to development; trainings on people-centred security and access to gender justice conducted with Women Development Department, Social Welfare and Human Rights Departments in Balochistan and KP respectively].
2.1: Scale 2: [Policies/regulations developed but not implemented, support provided for implementation of provincial SWD, LG and HR policies/plans; gender desks established in Balochistan and KP - basic legal aid provided to most vulnerable and at-risk women, girls and transgender persons]. 
2.2: Scale 2: [Provincial HRIMS stakeholders provided capacity development support; Social inclusion and social protection measures (helplines, shelter homes, referral mechanisms continued in all four provinces; institutionalization of protection measures in partnership with Women Development and Social Welfare Departments].
3.1:Scale 2: [Programme on gender-justice and inclusion of persons with disabilities, and transgenders implemented in partnership with MoHR; community stabilization and people-centred security programme implemented in Balochistan; psycho social support and livelihood skills trainings provided to 200 men and 200 women]
4.1:Scale 2: [Integration Support Groups (ISGs) provided trainings on community engagement through civilian-led mechanisms for peace and tolerance for improved access to services of the most vulnerable and at-risk populations (particularly women, transgenders and youth].</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Scale item 2: Policies/regulations developed but not implemented (National Action Plan on business &amp; Human Rights developed and implementation initiated; NCHR work plan developed &amp; 25% recommendations implemented)
1.2: Scale item 2: Partial Capacity(Human Rights Information Management System operationalized; Inter-Provincial Working Group operationalized)
2.1: Scale Item 2: Policies/regulations developed but not implemented (Support for development/implementation of provinci al LG and HR policies/plans)
2.2: Scale Item 1: Very Basic Capacity(Provincial data systems developed in all four provinces; staff trained on data entry and reporting; LG staff trained on inclusive service delivery in KP and Balochistan)
3.1: Scale Item 2: Partial capacity (Institutional digitization programme for inclusive, transparent and accountable service delivery designed for target district in all four provinces; Psycho social support and economic empowerment programme rolled out for 3000 (50% women) vulnerable and at-risk youth in all four provinces
4.1: Scale Item 2: Very Partial Capacity(Integration Support Groups (ISGs) assisting Social Welfare Departments in 3 target districts each in Sindh, KP and Punjab; partially improved engagement between CSOs and government for improved access to services of the most vulnerable and at-risk populations (particularly women, transgenders and youth)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Scale item 2: Policies/regulations developed but not implemented-Nationwide consultations conducted with government, civil society and private sector stakeholders for development of draft National Action Plan; continued support provided to NCHR to implement 25% recommendations as per 2 year work plan.
1.2: Scale item 2: Partial Capacity-HRIMS servers installed in all four provinces; linkages established with federal HRIMS
2.1: Scale Item 2: Yes, Support provided to HR, LG and Social Welfare departments; however delays due to COVID-19 in implementation of provincial plans.
2.2: Scale Item 1: Very Basic Capacity development exercises conducted in KP for HRIMS staff; LG and SWD staff training on inclusive service delivery (twinning) and gender-based planning and budgeting
3.1:Scale Item 2: Partial capacity- COVID-19 task established to develop a road-map for inclusive local governance in line with the UN&#x2019;s soc-economic assessment; psycho-social support and economic empowerment programme implemented in Swat and Multan; gender desks established in NMAs, Swat, Multan and Karachi
4.1:Scale Item 2: Very Partial Capacity: ISGs established and linked with local administration for increased awareness and oversight of development initiatives; helplines for psycho-social support to vulnerable and at-risk populations established in partnership with local government and civil society actors</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Scale item 3: Policies/regulations developed and partially implemented (National Action Plan approved by competent authority and implementation of short-term recommendations initiated; support provided to NHRIs, including NCHR,
NCRC, NCSW; technical assistance provided to implement policies targeting vulnerable groups, particularly persons with disabilities)
1.2: Scale item 2: Partial Capacity(Human Rights Information Management System operationalized; Inter-Provincial Working Group operationalized)
2.1: Scale Item 2: Policies/regulations developed but not implemented (Support provided for development/implementation of provincial LG and HR policies/plans)
2.2: Scale Item 2: Partial Capacity (Provincial HRIMS stakeholders provided capacity development support; Social
inclusion and social protection measures (helplines, shelter homes, referral mechanisms) established in all four
provinces; institutionalization of protection measures in partnership with LG and SW Departments)
3.1: Scale Item 2: Partial capacity (Implementation of short-term recommendations of the socioeconomic assessment and COVID-19 task-force recommendations; programme on gender-justice and inclusion of persons with disabilities, and transgenders rolled-out; community stabilization programme implemented in Balochistan and discussions with government
stakeholders on institutional of the model at the local level initiated)
4.1: Scale Item 2: Very Partial Capacity(Integration Support Groups (ISGs) assisting Social Welfare Departments in 3 target districts each in Sindh, KP and Punjab; partially improved engagement between CSOs and government for improved access to services of the most vulnerable and at-risk populations (particularly women, transgenders and youth)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Scale item 2: Policies/regulations developed but not implemented-Nationwide consultations conducted with government, civil society and private sector stakeholders- draft National Action plan developed and launched; continued support provided to NCHR to implement 25% recommendations as per 2 year work plan.
1.2: Scale item 2: Partial Capacity-HRIMS servers installed in all four provinces; linkages established with federal HRIMS. Inter-provincial working group on human rights established
2.1: Scale Item 2: Yes, Support provided to HR, LG and Social Welfare Departments; however, delays due to COVID-19 in implementation of provincial plans.
2.2: Scale Item 1: Very Basic Capacity development exercises conducted in Sindh, Balochistan, Punjab and KP for HRIMS staff; LG and SWD staff training on inclusive service delivery (twinning) and gender-based planning and budgeting. Transgender centre established in Islamabad.
3.1: Scale Item 2: Partial capacity- COVID-19 taskforce initiated implementation for inclusive response to Covid-19 in line with the UN&#x2019;s soc-economic assessment; psycho-social support and economic empowerment programme implemented in Swat and Multan; gender desks established in NMAs, Swat, Multan and Karachi
4.1: Scale Item 2: Very Partial Capacity: ISGs established and linked with local administration for increased awareness and oversight of development initiatives; helplines for psycho-social support to vulnerable and at-risk populations established in partnership with local government and civil society actors; implementation of LLDR model initiated in Quetta</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
